# Wave A cross-cutting unblocks: backtick-quoted identifiers (table & column
# names), the inline `col TYPE PRIMARY KEY` constraint form, and a UUID primary
# key (PK types beyond int/string/bool). The `#`-comment-skip in the test runner
# is exercised implicitly by this very comment block sitting inside the case.

-CASE WaveAUnblocks
-STATEMENT CREATE NODE TABLE `My Table`(id INT64 PRIMARY KEY, `full name` STRING)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:`My Table` {id: 1, `full name`: 'Ada Lovelace'})
---- ok
# a comment line in the middle of a case must not break the next statement
-STATEMENT MATCH (n:`My Table`) RETURN n.`full name`, n.id
---- 1
Ada Lovelace|1
-STATEMENT CREATE NODE TABLE U(uid UUID PRIMARY KEY, name STRING)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:U {uid: UUID('a0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380a11'), name: 'x'})
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (u:U) WHERE u.uid = UUID('a0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380a11') RETURN u.name
---- 1
x
